Later, Isuzu entered a more substantial model-exchange alliance with [[Honda]]. Among other models, it encompassed the rebadging of the [[Honda Accord#Fifth generation (1994)|Honda Accord]] sedan as the Isuzu Aska. This model was presented in March 1994, after stock of the Legacy-based, previous generation Aska had been sold out. The only difference to the Accord was the grille and logos.

It was only offered with a two-liter four-cylinder engine, combined with a four-speed automatic transmission. The model code assigned to it by Isuzu was '''CJ1'''. Production came to an end in September 1997, with sales from stock continuing for another two months.

